      "She woke up at four in the morning because her left arm had gone completely numb.",
      "Sam sat up on the narrow army cot, careful not to wake Orpheus, who was slumped in a canvas folding chair near the cellar stairs with a shotgun across his knees, or Fourfootyest, who was curled on a padded tool mat beneath the main console, his cybernetic eye powered down to a faint amber standby dot while his furry chest rose and fell in ragged, twitching sleep.",
      "Keeping her movements silent, Sam walked into the tiny subterranean washroom at the back of the basement and pulled the brass chain on the bare overhead bulb.",
      "She leaned over the stained porcelain sink, turned on the cold tap, and splashed water onto her face. When she looked up into the cracked mirror above the basin, she froze, gripping the edges of the sink until her knuckles ached.",
      "She rolled up the left sleeve of her flannel shirt.",
      "Running up the pale skin of her inner forearm, from her wrist all the way to the crook of her elbow, the veins weren't blue anymore. They were jet-black, flat, and slightly raised beneath the skin—hard and ribbon-like to the touch, with the unmistakable, smooth sheen of quarter-inch magnetic recording tape.",
      "When she pressed her right thumb against the dark vein at her wrist, she didn't feel a pulse. She felt a tiny, steady mechanical vibration, like a capstan motor pulling tape at 7.5 inches per second.",
      "\"No, no, no,\" she whispered to her reflection.",
      "Except the voice that came out of her throat wasn't entirely hers. At the very end of the third \"no,\" her vocal cords hitched, dropping an octave into a dry crackle of analog hiss, as if someone had bumped the microphone plug in her windpipe.",
      "She clapped both hands over her mouth, staring into her own eyes in the mirror. In the dim light of the washroom bulb, deep behind her dark pupils, a faint horizontal tracking line rolled slowly from the bottom of her irises to the top.",
      "And then came the pull.",
      "It wasn't a headache this time. It felt like a physical piece of copper wire had been fishhooked directly behind her left optical nerve and pulled taut by a winch miles away. Without her wanting to, her chin tugged roughly to the right, turning her head away from the mirror to stare straight at the western brick wall of the basement.",
      "Through three feet of earth, concrete, and copper mesh, she could feel it—a towering, three-legged colossus of red and white steel rising out of the fog atop Mount Sutro at the geographic center of the city.",
      "Sutro Tower.",
      "The entity was done playing with street-corner repeaters and subway platforms. Every Carrier in the Mission, SOMA, and the Tenderloin was linking up to feed a single, massive line of power straight up Clarendon Heights into the main broadcast array at the top of the mountain.",
      "The washroom door creaked open behind her.",
      "Fourfootyest stood on the threshold on his hind paws, his red optical lens clicking softly as it focused on the black, tape-like veins crawling up Sam’s bare forearm. He didn't bark an alarm, and he didn't reach for the stun baton on his belt. For a long moment, the little cybernetic dog just looked at her arm, then down at his own bionic steel claws where metal met scarred flesh.",
      "\"Hurts like hell when the wiring starts replacing the meat, doesn't it?\" his vocoder whispered, set to its lowest volume so Orpheus wouldn't hear.",
