      "Driving up Clarendon Avenue toward the summit of Mount Sutro felt like driving into the throat of a dead television set.",
      "The famous San Francisco fog hadn't just rolled in off the Pacific; it had curdled into a thick, oily gray soup that smelled of hot bakelite and ozone. As Orpheus pushed the old Volvo up the steep, winding grade through the eucalyptus forest, the trees lining the road seemed to jitter in and out of existence, their wet bark flickering with horizontal bands of white static.",
      "Above the treeline, the three mammoth red-and-white legs of Sutro Tower disappeared into the glowing purple clouds, humming so loudly that the windshield of the Volvo vibrated like a drumhead.",
      "\"Cut the headlights,\" Fourfootyest hissed from the passenger seat, his red optical lens dilated wide as it scanned the fog through the windshield in infrared. \"Two hundred yards ahead. The perimeter fence is crawling with them.\"",
      "Orpheus killed the lights and eased the car onto the muddy shoulder beneath a grove of overhanging eucalyptus trees, shutting off the ignition.",
      "Through the swirling gray mist ahead, Sam could see the chain-link security fence surrounding the base of the tower’s massive concrete foundations. Standing shoulder-to-shoulder along the outside of the fence were dozens—no, hundreds—of Carriers. They stood completely still in the dripping fog, their faces tilted up toward the humming steel legs above, their mouths slightly open as a low, harmonized sixty-hertz chord vibrated from their throats in a single, unbroken wall of sound.",
      "\"They’re acting as a human step-up transformer,\" Sam whispered, clutching her left arm as the black magnetic veins beneath her sleeve throbbed in sympathy with the choir outside. \"If they hear us, they’ll tear us apart.\"",
      "\"They won't hear us over their own carrier wave if we stay out of phase,\" Fourfootyest said, reaching down with his bionic claws to twist the dial on the heavy copper jammer strapped to his chest. A soft, counter-harmonic hum radiated from his vest, creating a five-foot bubble of dead air around the three of them that canceled out the deafening drone of the mountain. \"Stay inside my radius. One step outside the bubble, and you'll light up on their grid like a flare.\"",
      "They slipped out of the car and moved in a tight triangle through the dripping brush toward the eastern corner of the perimeter fence, where a drainage culvert ran beneath the chain-link.",
      "Fourfootyest went first, dropping to all fours just long enough to dart silently through the wet ferns before popping back up on his hind legs at the fence line. With two quick, silent squeezes of the fiberglass bolt cutters—Orpheus providing the leverage while Fourfootyest guided the jaws—they severed the bottom links of the fence, peeled back the wire, and bellied through the mud onto the tower grounds.",
      "Ten yards to their left, a Carrier in a soaked postman’s uniform stood staring at the sky, ribbons of black magnetic tape weeping from his eyes and tangling into the wet chain-link fence. He didn't even blink as they slipped past him toward the heavy steel service door of the main transmitter building at the base of the tower's legs.",
      "The electronic keypad beside the service door was melted into a slag of bubbling plastic and sparking wires. Fourfootyest stepped up to the seam of the steel door, extended a tiny plasma torch built into his right index claw, and sliced through the magnetic latch with a hiss of orange sparks.",
      "Orpheus caught the heavy door before it could clang open, ushered Sam and Fourfootyest inside, and eased it shut behind them."
