    "paragraphs": [
      "Sam hauled herself through the circular steel hatch at the very top of the central leg, tumbling onto the rubberized floor of the Primary Switching Vault.",
      "This was the brain of Sutro Tower’s original 1973 analog architecture—a cramped, octagonal chamber packed wall-to-wall with massive brass knife switches, pressurized nitrogen waveguide pipes, and a thick, four-inch trunk of solid braided copper running up through the center of the ceiling toward the antenna spires outside.",
      "Above the trunk line, a vintage green-phosphor military terminal—looking strangely out of place among the commercial television gear—flashed in urgent block letters:",
      "PRIMARY CAPACITOR LOAD: 98% TIME TO FULL SPECTRUM LOCK: 00:00:18",
      "Sam scrambled to her feet, unstrapping the three-foot fiberglass bolt cutters from her back. Her left eye was completely blind with static now, and the black tape-veins had crept all the way up her neck, pulsing against her carotid artery like cold fingers.",
      "She stepped up to the massive four-inch copper trunk line in the center of the room, opened the heavy steel jaws of the bolt cutters as wide as they would go, and wedged them around the braided conduit, throwing her entire body weight against the fiberglass handles.",
      "Ten feet away, the air near the ceiling vents suddenly imploded with a violet flash and a smell of singed wet wool.",
      "Fourfootyest crashed out of the collapsing spatial rift, bouncing hard off a steel equipment rack and skidding across the rubber floor in a tangle of smoking copper wire and scorched fur. The jammer on his chest was melted into a blackened lump of slag, the left ear of his furry head was singed black, and the brass vocoder on his collar was sparking intermittently.",
      "He raised his head, his single remaining canine eye going wide as his red optical lens spun wildly, scanning the green military terminal above Sam’s head and the strange, inverted grounding glyphs stamped into the lead shielding around the copper trunk line.",
      "\"Sam—wait!\" his damaged vocoder crackled, spitting sparks as he scrambled desperately across the floor on three limbs, his right bionic claw melted into a fused club. \"Don't cut it! Look at the terminal headers—we read the 1970s schematics upside down! This line isn't transmitting out from the tower—it’s pumping an inverted phase wave down into the bedrock!\"",
      "Sam was already mid-heave, her boots braced against the steel housing, the roar of the sixty-hertz hum in her skull completely drowning out the first half of his broken voice.",
      "\"Don't cut the trunk!\" Fourfootyest screamed, lunging for her ankle. \"The tower isn't a transmitter—it’s a cage!\"",
      "CLANG.",
      "With every ounce of strength left in her body, Sam slammed the fiberglass handles together.",
      "The hardened steel jaws bit straight through the four-inch braided copper trunk line.",
      "There was no explosion. Instead, all the sound in the universe simply stopped.",
      "The two severed ends of the massive copper conduit curled back like cut snakes, bleeding a brief shower of pale blue sparks that floated lazily to the rubber floor and died. The deafening sixty-hertz vibration that had been shaking Mount Sutro to its foundations vanished in a heartbeat.",
      "Sam collapsed backward onto her knees, dropping the bolt cutters, gasping for air in the sudden, eerie quiet. She blinked—and to her shock, the green static in her left eye cleared. The black veins in her wrist faded from raised magnetic tape back to dull, bruised gray.",
      "\"I did it,\" she breathed, looking over at Fourfootyest with a shaky, exhausted smile. \"The signal stopped.\"",
      "Fourfootyest didn't smile back. He was staring up at the vintage military CRT terminal above the severed conduit, the fur across his shoulders trembling.",
      "On the screen, the green text had turned blood-red.",
      "WARNING: PRIMARY GROUNDING CONDUIT SEVERED. PROJECT DARK REEL SUPPRESSION ARRAY: OFFLINE. PENINSULA CONTAINMENT FIELD COLLAPSING IN 3... 2... 1...",
      "Deep beneath their feet—not in the tower, not even in the mountain, but miles down in the ancient fault lines beneath the San Francisco Bay—something massive shifted in the dark, let out a low, sub-audible sigh that shook the entire tectonic plate, and woke up."
    ],
