      "The silence lasted less than four seconds.",
      "Then, from the severed lower half of the copper conduit—the side connected to the earth below, not the antennas above—a geyser of pitch-black, viscous static erupted straight up into the ceiling of the vault.",
      "Sutro Tower hadn't been broadcasting the entity across the Bay; for fifty years, the tower had been pumping a massive, three-pronged electromagnetic suppression wave down into the San Andreas fault line to keep a primordial tear pinned beneath the peninsula. The small street ruptures over the last two weeks had just been leaks through a cracking dam.",
      "And Sam had just blown the dam wide open.",
      "\"Down the shaft! Now!\" Fourfootyest roared, grabbing the strap of the bolt cutters with his good left claw and vaulting onto Sam’s shoulder as the steel walls of the Switching Vault began to peel backward like curling wallpaper, revealing a howling void of cyan and purple television snow behind the metal.",
      "Sam dove through the floor hatch and slid down the vertical iron ladder inside the tower leg, her leather gloves smoking from the friction against the rails.",
      "Around them, the interior of the tower was unmaking itself. Without the suppression wave holding local reality in calibration, the steel trusses and maintenance landings were flickering between 2026 and 1973—rust vanishing from bolts, wet paint appearing on beams, ghostly silhouettes of seventies linemen in hardhats flickering through the rungs like double-exposed photographs.",
      "When they hit the landing at Level 2, where the corridor had swallowed Orpheus ten minutes earlier, Sam skidded to a halt in front of the fused steel fire door.",
      "The wire-glass window was no longer black. Inside the auxiliary hallway, the sepia time-loop was spinning violently out of control, flashing like a strobe light—Orpheus lunging for the door, snapping back, lunging, snapping back, three frames a second—while the walls of the room dissolved into raw green phosphor gridlines around him.",
      "\"How do we break the frame?!\" Sam yelled over the groaning of the twisting tower legs.",
      "Fourfootyest leaped off her shoulder onto the fused door handle. His chest jammer was melted slag, but the copper coils inside it were still surging with residual capacitive charge from the 440-volt busbar blast.",
      "\"Back up two steps!\" the little cyborg snarled.",
      "He braced his hind paws against the cinderblock wall, jammed his melted, clubbed right metal claw directly into the exposed core of his own ruined chest rig to bridge the last undamaged capacitor, and slammed his left claw onto the steel doorframe.",
      "A raw, unmodulated pulse of jagged electromagnetic feedback ripped out of Fourfootyest’s harness and into the door.",
      "The wire-glass window shattered outward like a gunshot. Inside the room, the sepia film reel snapped with an audible twang, shattering the three-frame loop like a pane of sugar glass.",
      "Orpheus stumbled forward in real time, crashing straight through the buckled steel door into the corridor as if no time had passed at all since he’d lunged for the handle—only to look up in horror at Sam’s terrified face and Fourfootyest smoking on the floor.",
      "\"The array—\" Orpheus gasped, coughing ozone smoke.",
      "\"Was a dampener!\" Sam yelled, hauling Orpheus up by his coat while scooping the exhausted, sparking Lhasa Apso under her right arm. \"We didn't turn it off, Orpheus—we let it out! Run!\"",
      "They tore down the remaining flights of the concrete stairwell and burst out the lower service doors into the eucalyptus forest just as all three nine-hundred-foot legs of Sutro Tower lit up with a blinding, silent pillar of cyan light that punched straight through the fog bank into the stratosphere."
