      "They hit Clarendon Avenue in the Volvo on two wheels, tires screaming against the wet asphalt as Orpheus threw the wagon into a controlled skid down the mountain toward Portola Drive.",
      "When they rounded the hairpin curve at Twin Peaks, where the trees opened up to reveal the panoramic view of the entire city of San Francisco below, Sam pressed her hands against the dashboard and couldn't breathe.",
      "The city hadn't gone dark. That would have been a mercy.",
      "Every single window in every high-rise from the Financial District to the Civic Center, every digital billboard along the highway, every streetlight, traffic signal, and apartment television across the seven-by-seven-mile peninsula had locked onto the exact same color: a blinding, dead-channel cyan glare.",
      "Down in the grid of the Mission and Market Street, the amber headlights of cars had stopped moving. Out of the apartment buildings, the bars, the BART stations, and the office towers, tens of thousands of people were walking calmly out into the middle of the streets.",
      "Even from a mile up on the slopes of Twin Peaks, with the car windows rolled up, they could hear it.",
      "A hundred thousand human throats, standing shoulder to shoulder from the Embarcadero to the Castro, had tilted their heads back toward the cyan sky and begun to hum a single, harmonized sixty-hertz chord. The vibration was so massive that the suspension cables of the Bay Bridge in the distance were visibly oscillating like giant harp strings, adding a deep, metallic sub-bass drone that rattled the steering wheel in Orpheus’s hands.",
      "\"Where do we go?\" Sam whispered, watching a wave of cyan static roll down Market Street like a tidal wave of glowing fog. \"The Tenderloin bunker is right in the middle of the grid! Copper mesh won't hold against a city-wide harmonic!\"",
      "In the backseat, Fourfootyest was busy wrapping emergency insulating tape around his fused right paw with his teeth and his good left claw.",
      "\"Not the Tenderloin,\" Orpheus said grimly, cutting hard right onto Woodside Avenue and flooring the accelerator north toward Golden Gate Park and the coast. \"When you cut that line, the terminal flashed a project name, didn't it?\" \"Project Dark Reel,\" Sam said immediately. \"It was on the military terminal in the vault.\"",
      "Orpheus exchanged a dark look with Fourfootyest in the rearview mirror.",
      "\"In 1977, the US Army Signal Corps decommissioned a subterranean coastal defense annex under the bluffs of the Presidio, right beside the Golden Gate,\" Orpheus said, weaving past three abandoned cars stopped diagonally across Park Presidio Boulevard while their drivers stood on the median strip, staring at the sky. \"It was built inside forty feet of lead-lined, pre-atomic concrete beneath Battery Blaney to monitor deep-trench submarine cables—and whatever else they found under the fault line when they built Sutro Tower. If there’s an instruction manual for putting the lid back on this thing, it’s locked in that vault.\""
