      "Before Fourfootyest could even reach for his plasma torch, the thermometer bolted to the concrete pillar beside them dropped thirty degrees in two seconds, the red alcohol column plunging to the bottom of the glass until the bulb cracked.",
      "Sam’s breath misted white in the flashlight beams.",
      "Across the room, the sealed steel bulkhead of BAY 2 didn't open—the concrete floor directly in front of it simply split apart.",
      "A jagged fissure of blinding purple-and-cyan television static tore through the three-foot-thick reinforced slab, accompanied by the deafening, bone-shattering roar of a giant reel-to-reel tape deck spinning backward at a thousand miles an hour.",
