      "It was six feet tall and impossibly broad, dragging itself forward with a heavy, wet, metallic clatter. It was the original 1977 Signal Corps engineering team from Bay 2—not six men anymore, but a single, horrifying First-Generation Carrier fused together over half a century inside the fault line. Rotting olive-drab military fatigues were woven seamlessly into thick bundles of oxidized copper wiring and exposed human ribcages; where a single head should have been, three overlapping skulls fused at the temples stared out through six glowing vacuum-tube eyes, while brass Ampex tape heads spun frantic, clicking circles inside its open, shared jaw.",
