      "They burst out of the sunken concrete bunker of Battery Blaney into the Presidio fog, Orpheus and Sam slamming the three-foot-thick lead-lined airlock door shut and spinning the rusted iron hand-wheel until the locking dogs engaged with a heavy *thud*.",
      "Three seconds later, something massive slammed against the inside of the blast door from below, vibrating the sandy earth under their boots and sending a hairline crack straight up the moss-covered concrete archway. Thick black magnetic tape began to squeeze out through the microscopic gap around the rubber door gasket like pressurized grease.",
      "\"That lock’s gonna hold for maybe ten minutes before the pressure equalizes,\" Fourfootyest panted, hopping into the back of the 1988 Volvo wagon as Orpheus keyed the ignition. The little cybernetic Lhasa Apso’s fur was matted with soot, his right bionic paw was still fused into a blunt steel club from Sutro Tower, and his brass vocoder clicked with every ragged breath. \"Where to now, boss? We’re running out of century-old bunkers.\"",
      "Orpheus threw the wagon into reverse, backing hard down the gravel service road onto Lincoln Boulevard above the cliffs of the Golden Gate.",
      "Through the windshield, as the coastal fog parted in the morning wind, the view of the Marin Headlands across the strait made Sam’s stomach drop.",
      "Across the churning gray water, the two seven-hundred-foot orange-vermilion towers of the Golden Gate Bridge were wrapped in a shimmering, aurora-like corona of dead-channel cyan light. Tens of thousands of Carriers had walked out onto the pedestrian walkways of the bridge from the San Francisco toll plaza, standing shoulder to shoulder from the south anchorage all the way to the center span, their hands pressed flat against the thick vertical steel suspender ropes.",
      "They were turning the entire suspension bridge into a mile-long harp antenna, using the steel cables to bounce the peninsula’s sixty-hertz signal across the water toward Marin County.",
      "\"It’s trying to jump the strait,\" Orpheus said grimly, pulling the Volvo behind a grove of thick Monterey cypress trees overlooking the old Fort Winfield Scott parade grounds, hidden from the main road. He left the engine idling in neutral and turned around in his seat to look at Sam.",
      "Sam sat huddled in the passenger seat, cradling her burned left palm against her flannel shirt. The skin across her fingers was branded with the backward imprint of an Ampex erase head, and the black magnetic veins now reached the base of her jaw. Yet her head was clearer than it had been in days; the shock of reversing the current in the vault had temporarily burned away the fog behind her left eye.",
      "In the backseat, Fourfootyest set the dusty 1977 leather logbook and the ten-inch aluminum reel of quarter-inch Ampex magnetic tape down on top of an ammo crate.",
      "\"We don't have a ten-inch reel-to-reel deck in the wagon to play that,\" Orpheus said, pointing at the aluminum spool. \"Unless you can wire a step-down head off the car’s alternator.\"",
      "\"Don't need a deck,\" Fourfootyest rasped, his red camera-aperture eye zooming in on the white grease-pencil label written across the aluminum flange of the reel: `PROJECT DARK REEL — CALIBRATION MASTER — 19.8 HZ INVERTED — DO NOT ERASE`.",
      "The little cyborg dog looked up from the reel to Sam’s scarred left hand.",
