      "Orpheus reached across the center console, his gloved hand hovering an inch from Sam’s shoulder. \"If that tape is corrupted by the fault line, it’ll overwrite whatever is left of your nervous system on the spot. Wait until I can rig a buffer circuit—\"",
      "\"There isn't time for a buffer circuit,\" Sam said quietly, looking out the windshield at the glowing cyan corona climbing the south tower of the Golden Gate Bridge. \"If that signal crosses into Marin, it has the entire North American landmass. No water breaks, no fault lines to hold it back.\"",
      "She reached into the backseat, pinched the brown magnetic ribbon between her burned left thumb and index finger, took a slow breath, and pulled the tape steadily across the raw nerve endings of her palm."
